  "note": "A Bn delaying on successive posns, its normal method on the wide frontages of a delay (MIB s28 para 6 a p 233; OOW3 s6 pp 28-32: trade space for time, inflict maximum destruction, avoid decisive engagement). The click is the Bn HQ on the first delaying posn (DP 1); the aim is the way back, the second click the last delaying posn (DP 3, planned), DP 2 half way. On each posn all Coys forward and a small reserve placed to check penetrations and cover the rearward move; the gaps covered by patrols, OPs and LPs (MIB s28 para 13 a-c pp 238-239); successive posns far enough apart that the En must regroup and redeploy his close support weapons (MIB para 12 c pp 237-238: here the En 81 mm Mor, 4.2 km, ORBAT); phase lines with a stated time (para 12 d p 238); the echelons behind the next delaying posn (para 13 d p 239). How long each posn holds is the higher Comd's to say (OOW3 s6 para 6 a p 29). Battle Posns are drawn turned to face the En behind the plan.",
